+// map_district_assign — the nearest-anchor district of an arbitrary TILE
+// (integer grid coordinates): the district whose anchor minimizes the
+// scaled Euclidean squared distance (MAP_ANCHOR_SCALE = 10 — the anchor's
+// f32 tile pos scales to tenths before the compare; ODN-10: pure integer
+// math, no transcendentals). Tie-break = the LOWER district index (strict
+// less keeps the first — file order, deterministic). The load-time
+// partition (district_tiles) uses the same proc + scale, so the SEED
+// draw's district and the ATTACH cluster's district label agree with the
+// baked assignment BY CONSTRUCTION (one definition, no drift).
+map_district_assign :: proc(b: ^Map_Board, pos: [2]i32) -> u16 {
+	best_d: u16 = 0
+	best_d2: i64 = 0
+	for d in 0..<len(b.districts) {
+		ax := i32(math.round(f64(b.districts[d].pos[0]) * MAP_ANCHOR_SCALE))
